Thanks for the review, @yewentao256.

@WoosukKwon @njhill, could one of you take a look for approval? The change is confined to `_dummy_sampler_run` in `vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py` (+8/-3): the profiler now runs the logits-processing pipeline in fp32 with the params the warm-up uses, so the KV-cache sizing accounts for the memory the sampler warm-up actually needs (the 594 MiB `[num_reqs x vocab]` fp32 tensor that makes `main` OOM at startup on L4 / A10G / A100-40GB; same-command repro, lm_eval gsm8k and `vllm bench serve` logs for `main` vs this branch are in https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/57926#issuecomment-5988390978).

On the unit test: no objection to dropping `tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_model_runner_v2_sampler_profiling.py` as @yewentao256 suggested so the diff stays code-only; I will push that as soon as the direction is confirmed.

